-- title:
--   Coefficient extension commutes with the ℓ-adic Drinfeld curve representation
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $k$ a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ (`GaloisField q 2`), such that the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k`, the quotient of $k[x_0,x_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`, is a domain; let $F =$ `drinfeldFunctionField q k` be its fraction field, and let $\mathrm{Pic}^0 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0 k F`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L223) be the group of degree-zero divisors on the places of $F/k$ modulo principal divisors. Let $\ell$ be a prime and put $V = \mathbb{Q}_\ell \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\ell} T_\ell(\mathrm{Pic}^0)$, where $T_\ell(M)$ is the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $M$ with $\ell^n x_n = 0$ and $\ell x_{n+1} = x_n$. The group $H =$ `hSubgroup q`, the kernel of the character `hChar q` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$, acts on $F$ over $k$ through `hFunctionFieldAction q k`, hence on $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ and on $V$ via [`ModularCurve.rationalGaloisRep`](def/ModularCurve_JZeroTateModule.html#L48). Let $E$ and $E'$ be fields over $\mathbb{Q}_\ell$ with $E'$ an $E$-algebra forming a scalar tower over $\mathbb{Q}_\ell$, and let $\rho_E$ and $\rho_{E'}$ be the representations of $H$ on $E \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}_\ell} V$ and $E' \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}_\ell} V$ obtained from the above action of $H$ on $V$ by base change. The assertion is that there exists an $E'$-linear isomorphism $e : E' \otimes_E (E \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}_\ell} V) \to E' \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}_\ell} V$ with $e \circ (\rho_E(h) \otimes \mathrm{id}_{E'}) = \rho_{E'}(h) \circ e$ for every $h \in H$.
--
--   This is the transitivity of coefficient extension for the $\ell$-adic representation of the group $H$ on the rational Tate module of the Jacobian of the Drinfeld curve: iterating base change from $\mathbb{Q}_\ell$ to $E$ and then to $E'$ agrees, equivariantly, with base change directly to $E'$. It is used in the analysis of the $H$-representation on this Tate module, specifically by [`DrinfeldCurve.slEquivariant_quadratic_of_isCuspidalOfType_of_perfectField`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.slEquivariant_quadratic_of_isCuspidalOfType_of_perfectField), where one is free to enlarge the coefficient field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_exists_linearEquiv_rationalTateModule_baseChange_comp_eq.lean

